      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "From 404 patients with acute myocardial infarction, 14 (3%) had coronary lesions considered not obstructive (lesion < 70%) and 4 had chronic Chagas's disease. This study suggests that acute myocardial infarction without coronary obstruction had particular feature in the Brazilian population."},
